Skins also have the option of having either 3 or 4 pixel wide arms, which can be changed on the profile page as well.<ref>{{tweet|MojangSupport|511889676227989504|Slim-armed skins are now available to all! Visit http://minecraft.net/profile to make changes, or https://help.mojang.com/customer/portal/articles/979200-minecraft-skins for help! ^MW|September 16, 2014}}</ref>

The {{cd|steve.png}} and {{cd|alex.png}} files in [[client.jar]] can also be changed and replaced via a resource pack, but the effects are visible only to players using the resource pack, and affects all players with the default skin.

=== ''Bedrock Edition'' ===
[[File:Dressing Room (Bedrock).png|thumb|The Dressing Room]]
Players can choose one of the nine default skins upon first launch or in the [[Dressing Room]] when creating from an empty slot. The Dressing Room, accessible from the [[main menu]], [[profile]], and [[Game Menu|game menu]], can also be used to switch skins, change, or remove skins from five available slots.

In the "Classic Skins" tab, players can switch to a downloaded or owned skin. Skins can be obtained as part of [[skin packs]] in the [[Marketplace]], purchased using [[Minecoins]]. The player has to sign in to their Microsoft (or their respective console account on PlayStation/Nintendo) to access all the skins they owned and bought from the Marketplace, on any device.

On Windows and mobile devices, custom skin files can be imported in the "Classic Skins" tab, or manually in {{Cd|[[com.mojang]]/custom_skins}}. The player must select a valid skin image file from their file explorer/photo gallery (a {{cd|.png}} texture from 64x32, 64x64, or 128x128 pixels), and must choose between the two model sizes (classic/slim). Players can also make their own skin packs, which must include a {{cd|manifest.json}} file, a {{cd|skins.json}} file, and all the desired skins. An additional {{cd|.lang}} file can be added inside a folder labeled {{cd|texts}} to display the skin names, but the game can register the skins without it.

== Skin packs ==
{{main|Skin pack}}

Skin packs are collections of multiple wearable skins and available {{in|bedrock}} as downloadable content. They can be acquired through:
*The [[Marketplace]], which officially hosts a large number of skin packs by Mojang Studios and their partners. Most of them cost Minecoins (Tokens on PS4), but some have been released for free.
*The {{cd|.mcskin}} files put in the {{cd|skin_packs}} or {{cd|development_skin_packs}} folder in the game files (inaccessible on consoles).
*External sources such as community hosted repositories for skin packs, which are automatically imported with <code>.mcpack</code> files (not on consoles). For information about the contents of a custom skin pack, see {{Slink|Skin pack|Package format}}.

