* In April 2018, {{WP|malware}} code was discovered inside of several downloadable user-made ''Minecraft'' image skins for use with the {{JE}} of the game.<ref name="avastmalware">{{citation|url=https://blog.avast.com/minecraft-players-exposed-to-malicious-code-in-modified-skins|title=Minecraft players exposed to malicious code in modified “skins”|author=Alexej Savčin|website=blog.avast.com|date=April 17, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/0/https://blog.avast.com/minecraft-players-exposed-to-malicious-code-in-modified-skins}}</ref><ref name="pcgamermalware" /><ref name="varietymalware1" /> {{WP|Avast}} stated that nearly 50,000 accounts were infected, and when activated, the malware would attempt to {{WP|Disk formatting#Reformatting|reformat}} the user's hard drive.<ref name="varietymalware1">{{citation|author=Stefanie Fogel|date=18 April 2018|title=Nearly 50,000 'Minecraft' Accounts Infected With Malware Thanks to Modified 'Skins' |url=https://variety.com/2018/gaming/news/minecraft-malware-1202757936/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20201210205116/https://variety.com/2018/gaming/news/minecraft-malware-1202757936/ |archive-date=10 December 2020 |access-date=3 April 2021 |website={{WP|Variety (magazine)|Variety}} |publisher=Variety Media}}</ref><ref name="pcgamermalware">{{citation|author=Paul Lilly|date=18 April 2018 |title=Beware of malicious Minecraft skins that attempt to erase your hard drive |url=https://www.pcgamer.com/uk/beware-of-malicious-minecraft-skins-that-attempt-to-erase-your-hard-drive/ |url-status=live |website={{WP|PC Gamer}} |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210403155908/https://www.pcgamer.com/uk/beware-of-malicious-minecraft-skins-that-attempt-to-erase-your-hard-drive/ |archive-date=3 April 2021}}</ref> [[Mojang Studios|Mojang]] promptly patched the issue, and released a statement stating that "the code would not be run or read by the game itself",<ref name="pcgamermalware" /> and would run only when the image containing the skin itself was opened.<ref>{{citation |author=Stefanie Fogel|date=19 April 2018 |title='Minecraft' Developer Issues Fix for Skins Virus |url=https://variety.com/2018/gaming/news/minecraft-virus-skins-fix-1202761270/ |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180907125202/https://variety.com/2018/gaming/news/minecraft-virus-skins-fix-1202761270/ |archive-date=7 September 2018 |access-date=3 April 2021 |website={{WP|Variety (magazine)|Variety}} |publisher=Variety Media}}</ref>

